      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Nocturnal pains of the leg were the only complaint of a 2 1/2-year-old girl with recurrent dislocations of the left hip. Unusual movement during sleep probably caused the dislocations. This case represents a benign entity characterized by spontaneous or voluntary posterior dislocations of the femoral head in young children without other significant connective tissue abnormalities."},
